exports[`Lumen & Loom Studio > Strategy System › 1. Situation & Direction > tile strategy-foundation-0 1`] = `
"Current SituationCurrent SituationiLumen & Loom Studio Ltd was incorporated in March 2026 by Maya Chen, Oliver Grant and Priya Shah and opens its Hackney Wick studio in October 2026. We sell a handwoven homeware collection online and at London markets, run beginner weaving workshops, and are starting bespoke commissions and a trade collection for interior designers and boutique hotels. Customers find us through Instagram, markets, word of mouth and design fairs. We are funded by £13,000 of founders’ capital, a £15,000 Start Up Loan and an £8,000 Hackney grant (half received). Monthly fixed costs are about £7,500, mostly three modest director salaries and rent; revenue starts small and is expected to cover costs from around August 2027. An angel round of £20,000 is in preparation to close a funding gap before then.RefreshiBack‹›Current SituationSWOT AnalysisStrategic CompassStrategic PeriodBack
[fields] Lumen & Loom Studio Ltd was incorporated in March 2026 by Maya Chen, Oliver Grant and Priya Shah and opens its Hackney Wick studio in October 2026. We sell a handwoven homeware collection online and at London markets, run beginner weaving workshops, and are starting bespoke commissions and a trade collection for interior designers and boutique hotels. Customers find us through Instagram, markets, word of mouth and design fairs. We are funded by £13,000 of founders’ capital, a £15,000 Start Up Loan and an £8,000 Hackney grant (half received). Monthly fixed costs are about £7,500, mostly three modest director salaries and rent; revenue starts small and is expected to cover costs from around August 2027. An angel round of £20,000 is in preparation to close a funding gap before then."
`;

exports[`Lumen & Loom Studio > Strategy System › 1. Situation & Direction > tile strategy-foundation-1 1`] = `
"SWOT AnalysisSWOT AnalysisiStrengths1.Three complementary founders: craft, sales and operations2.Genuinely handmade in London with traceable British materials3.Two revenue types: products and workshops4.Lifetime repair service no competitor offersWeaknesses1.Limited production capacity (three looms)2.Cash runway of only a few months without new funding3.No trade track record yet4.Heavy reliance on Maya for weaving and teachingOpportunities1.Growing demand for sustainable, local interiors among designers and hotels2.Experience gifting and craft workshops booming in London3.Grant and SEIS-backed angel funding for creative businesses4.Retailer interest in UK-made homewareThreats1.Cost-of-living pressure on discretionary spending2.Rising wool and energy prices3.Larger brands launching “artisan” lines4.Rent review on the studio in 2028Back‹›Current SituationSWOT AnalysisStrategic CompassStrategic PeriodBack
[fields] Three complementary founders: craft, sales and operations | Genuinely handmade in London with traceable British materials | Two revenue types: products and workshops | Lifetime repair service no competitor offers | Limited production capacity (three looms) | Cash runway of only a few months without new funding | No trade track record yet | Heavy reliance on Maya for weaving and teaching | Growing demand for sustainable, local interiors among designers and hotels | Experience gifting and craft workshops booming in London | Grant and SEIS-backed angel funding for creative businesses | Retailer interest in UK-made homeware | Cost-of-living pressure on discretionary spending | Rising wool and energy prices | Larger brands launching “artisan” lines | Rent review on the studio in 2028"
`;

exports[`Lumen & Loom Studio > Strategy System › 1. Situation & Direction > tile strategy-foundation-2 1`] = `
"Strategic CompassStrategic CompassiBy 2030, Lumen & Loom is London’s best-known independent weaving studio: a team of eight makers, a collection stocked by twenty UK independents, commissions for boutique hotels across the UK, a workshop programme with a waiting list, and a fully traceable low-carbon supply chain. Profitable, and still making every piece by hand in Hackney.Back‹›Current SituationSWOT AnalysisStrategic CompassStrategic PeriodBack
