tionSplitMilestonesOtherUpfront (%)iRest AfteriAt the normal level: $4,500 a monthLeft from each project after its costs: $5,880Delivery: about 24 founders' hours a month and about 12 externalAssumptionsAssumptions: the first builds from May 2027; about 40% of audits turn into a build of two to four automations; average $7,500; 50% at signing and the rest on handover about two months later.▾3.Automation Care RetainerPriceiChargediMonthlySelectPer salePer projectMonthlyQuarterlyAnnuallyPrice ($)PerClientUnitProductProjectSessionParticipantHourDayClientLicenceSubscriptionOtherSales VolumeiActive Clientsi5from Demand & ConversionBuild-upiGradual build-upSelectSteady from the startGradual build-upMonth by monthFirst MonthiMonths to NormaliDemand & Conversion suggests about 22 months to reach nine tenths of it.Begins and PaymentiBeginsJuly 2027Customer PaysiWhen earnedWhen earnedUpfrontOn completionSplitMilestonesOtherAt the normal level: $6,000 a monthLeft from each client after its costs: $1,155Delivery: about 30 founders' hours a monthAssumptionsAssumptions: the first retainer client from July 2027, as builds are handed over; about 0.5 new clients a month and 10% cancelling level off at about five active clients within about 22 months; billed monthly.Revenue SummaryiRevenue StreamPriceExpected VolumeExpected RevenueShareAI Workflow Audit$2,500 / project1.5 / month$3,75026%Automation Build$7,500 / project0.6 / month$4,50032%Automation Care Retainer$1,200 / client, monthly5 active$6,00042%Total$14,250 / monthCan the Expected Sales Be Delivered?iFounderDelivery HoursRecurring WorkRemainingOther OfferingsBusiest MonthJordan Ellis96 h30 h66 h47 hApr 2029The expected sales fit the founders' capacity: at the busiest (Apr 2029), about 77 h of 96 h a month (80%)i.Delivered outside the founders' capacity: Freelance developer about 12 h a month at the busiest. Their cost is part of the Offering's costs.↓▾2.Break EveniFinancial RiskAvailable resources are expected to be exhausted